WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.207
Completeness and uniqueness are different problems.

00:00:03.207 --> 00:00:06.862
Completeness asks whether needed values are present.

00:00:06.862 --> 00:00:10.577
The seriousness depends on the field and the use case.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:16.067
Missing email may be acceptable while missing patient ID may be critical.

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:21.157
Uniqueness asks whether one real-world entity appears more than intended.

00:00:21.157 --> 00:00:24.362
Exact duplicate rows are easy to detect.

00:00:24.362 --> 00:00:31.137
Duplicate entities under different identifiers are harder and may require entity-resolution methods.

00:00:31.137 --> 00:00:35.222
Always distinguish missing information from repeated identity.

00:00:35.222 --> 00:00:39.512
In practice, quality rules should be tied to a use case.

00:00:39.512 --> 00:00:46.262
A fifteen-minute delay may be acceptable for a monthly report but unacceptable for a real-time alert.

00:00:46.262 --> 00:00:54.372
Likewise, an unusual physiological value should often be flagged and investigated rather than automatically

00:00:54.372 --> 00:00:58.238
deleted. Good cleaning preserves evidence and documents uncertainty.
